<p>First, find available output devices:</p>
<div class="highlight"><pre><span></span><code>$ mpv --audio-device=help
List of detected audio devices:
  'auto' (Autoselect device)
  'coreaudio/220EF936-0000-0000-0420-0104A5502178' (HP P34hc G4)
  'coreaudio/88-C9-E8-E7-8D-85:output' (skybert-WH-1000XM4)
  'coreaudio/BuiltInSpeakerDevice' (MacBook Pro Speakers)
  'avfoundation/220EF936-0000-0000-0420-0104A5502178' (HP P34hc G4)
  'avfoundation/88-C9-E8-E7-8D-85:output' (skybert-WH-1000XM4)
  'avfoundation/BuiltInSpeakerDevice' (MacBook Pro Speakers)
</code></pre></div>

<p>Then, specify the one you want in the call to <code>mpv</code>:</p>
<div class="highlight"><pre><span></span><code>$<span class="w"> </span>mpv<span class="w"> </span>--audio-device<span class="o">=</span><span class="s1">'coreaudio/88-C9-E8-E7-8D-85:output'</span><span class="w"> </span>file.mp3
</code></pre></div>

<p>Happy listening!</p>